    A15_SMSS_71_M016935_023                                                   
                                                                              
    Apollo 15 Soil Mechanics                                                  
    Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D2                          
                                                                              
    Post-Flight Penetration Calibration Plot                                  
                                                                              
    This handwritten plot gives the post-flight calibration numbers to        
    reduce the depth of penetration data recorded on drum S/N 2002 used on    
    flight unit S/N 2003 of the Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP)      
    carried on the Apollo 15 mission.  The plot gives the actual pentration   
    of the SRP in centimeters (ordinate) vs. the penetration in centimeters   
    recorded on the drum in centimeters (abscissa). Six tests on the          
    deadweight jig at the Manned Space Center in Houston give a linear        
    result, a second line above the first represents an additional 3.75 cm    
    of penetration for the initil SRP penetration, added to account for the   
    additional length of the cone attached to the bottom of the penetrometer  
    rod extending below the base plate. This plot, along with the Pre-Flight  
    Calibration information, was used to reduce the raw data taken from the   
    LSRP drum and calculate the actual penetration of the instrument into     
    the lunar surface.                                                        
                                                                              
